WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.728
Welcome to today's exercise. Here is how
to join, how your screen works,

2
00:00:05.728 --> 00:00:12.490
how to answer, how to send messages, and
what to do if something goes wrong.

3
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.650
First, the most important thing. This
exercise tests the plan, not individuals.

4
00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.450
Findings are reported at team level.

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.630
When this briefing ends, the room screen
shows a code.

6
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:34.910
Scan it with your phone's camera.

7
00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:41.220
On a laptop, or from somewhere else, open
the join link you were sent.

8
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:48.630
Enter your details, choose Participant,
tick the privacy box, and press Register.

9
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:56.940
Each inject appears on the room screen,
and a voice usually reads it aloud.

10
00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:01.269
On your phone, the Inject tab shows the
same message,

11
00:01:01.269 --> 00:01:04.310
the countdown, and your answer box.

12
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:08.800
The Messages tab is for talking to the
facilitator.

13
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:14.750
On a laptop, the inject and your messages
sit side by side.

14
00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:22.720
Most injects need one answer per
department, marked Group task.

15
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.080
Agree it together, and let one person
type.

16
00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:30.307
If that person's phone is busy or gone,

17
00:01:30.307 --> 00:01:34.420
press Take over, and the text so far comes
with you.

18
00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:38.710
Some injects are marked Individual task.

19
00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.840
Then everyone answers alone.

20
00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:46.210
Press Submit answer before the time runs
out.

21
00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:50.319
Until then, you can press Edit answer to
change it,

22
00:01:50.319 --> 00:01:53.360
and Submit changes to send it again.

23
00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.653
If you need more time, open Messages,

24
00:01:58.653 --> 00:02:02.680
tap We need a few more minutes, and press
Send.

25
00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:07.190
Or type your own message, and press Send.

26
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:11.840
Extra time, when given, is for everyone.

27
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:17.420
The facilitator's messages appear at the
top, with Reply and Got it.

28
00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.310
Took a call, or locked your screen?

29
00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:29.130
Nothing is lost. The page catches up by
itself.

30
00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:35.630
If your phone restarts, open the same link
and press Continue on Welcome back.

31
00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:38.910
Your typed text is still there.

32
00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:43.985
On a new phone or laptop, use the same
name and department,

33
00:02:43.985 --> 00:02:46.880
and press Yes, continue as me.

34
00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:50.435
Lost your page? Open the link again,

35
00:02:50.435 --> 00:02:54.870
or ask your room's Observer for the join
code.

36
00:02:55.420 --> 00:03:01.040
Use Do Not Disturb, not flight mode, and
stay plugged in if you can.

37
00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:06.630
At the end, please answer the one-minute
survey before you leave.

38
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:12.120
To recap. Scan the code or open the link.

39
00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.956
For a group task, one person types your
department's answer;

40
00:03:16.956 --> 00:03:20.720
for an individual task, everyone answers.

41
00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:26.920
Submit before the time runs out, and if
you lose your page, open the link again.

42
00:03:27.470 --> 00:03:31.450
Your facilitator will start the exercise
shortly.

